  "query_preview": "(Monday through Thursday)...\nHigh temperatures on Monday will cool another few to around 5\ndegrees with the greatest cooling for the inland valleys onto the\nthe coastal slopes of the mountains. High temperatures on Monday\nwill be as much as 5 to 10 degrees below average for the mountains\nand valleys with high temperatures ranging from the lower to mid\n70s near the coast to the upper 70s to mid 80s for the Inland \nEmpire with the lower deserts in the upper 90s.\n\nHigh pressure over Texas and northern Mexico is expected to bring\na warming trend beginning on Tuesday and continuing for much of \nthe rest of next week, though with increasing spread in just how \nmuch warming may occur. NBM has the greater warming for Tuesday \nand Wednesday with lesser additional warming for Thursday and \nFriday.\n\nHigh temperatures would warm to within a few degrees above and\nbelow average on Wednesday and to a few degrees above average on\nThursday. High temperatures on Thursday would range from the mid\nto upper 70s near the coast to the upper 80s to mid 90s for the \nInland Empire with 100 to 104 for the lower deserts. Dry weather\nis expected to continue through much of next week.",
